## Overview

SQL Injection (CWE-89) is one of the most dangerous web application vulnerabilities. It allows attackers to interfere with the queries an application makes to its database.

## Recommended Fix

Always use parameterised queries:

```typescript
// UNSAFE
const q = `SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = '${userId}'`;

// SAFE
const q = 'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1';
const result = await pool.query(q, [userId]);
```

## References
- [OWASP SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)
- [CWE-89](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)

## Overview

Cross-Site Scripting (CWE-79) allows attackers to inject client-side scripts into web pages. React's JSX auto-escapes by default, but `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` bypasses this protection.

## Recommended Fix

```tsx
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

function SafeHTML({ html }: { html: string }) {
  return <div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: DOMPurify.sanitize(html) }} />;
}
```

## References
- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)
- [CWE-79](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)

## Overview

CWE-287 (Improper Authentication) includes JWT algorithm confusion attacks where an attacker can forge tokens by exploiting permissive algorithm settings.

## Recommended Fix

```typescript
// UNSAFE
jwt.verify(token, secret, { algorithms: ['none'] });

// SAFE
jwt.verify(token, publicKey, { algorithms: ['RS256'], issuer: 'auth.example.com' });
```

## References
- [Auth0: Critical vulnerabilities in JSON Web Token libraries](https://auth0.com/blog/critical-vulnerabilities-in-json-web-token-libraries/)
- [CWE-287](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/287.html)
